PROVENANCE OF THIS REFERENCE — read before trusting its WER numbers.

The poem text is from "A Calendar of Sonnets" by Helen Hunt Jackson (1830-1885),
public domain, so those lines are independent of any transcription.

The LibriVox preamble ("read for LibriVox dot org by ...") was taken from the
base model's own output, because the reader's name and website are not in any
published text. That part is therefore NOT independent: a model that hears the
preamble the same way base did scores better than it should.

Consequence: treat WER on this clip as indicative, not authoritative. The
authoritative reference is the project owner's hand-written transcript of their
own recording, which no model has seen.

CONFIRMED IN PRACTICE (2026-09-26)
----------------------------------
This warning was not hypothetical. Comparing tiny/base/small/medium on the full
45 seconds gave medium 28.9% WER with 24 deletions — apparently the worst model
of the four. medium simply skips the spoken preamble and starts at the poem,
and the preamble is exactly the part of this reference that came from base.

Scored from the poem's first word, where the reference is Helen Hunt Jackson's
published text, the ranking reverses and medium is the best at 3.0%. See D-065.

Use --score-from to exclude the preamble:

    python scripts/benchmark_transcription.py \
        --audio samples/public/en_sonnet_january_45s.wav \
        --models tiny base small medium --language en --score-from winter
